From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AgentLand <agentland@localhost>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 23:22:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Endpoint options: relay TLS roots, fixed port, external
 addresses

- EndpointOptions.relay_tls_roots / EndpointBuilder.relay_tls_roots
  (iroh's Builder::ca_tls_config, as proposed in iroh-ffi PR #288):
  - RelayTlsRoots.custom trusts only the given DER certificates (a
    private CA, or a relay's self-signed certificate).
  - RelayTlsRoots.embeddedPlus trusts the Mozilla roots and the given
    certificates, so one endpoint can use a relay with a private
    certificate and publicly trusted relays (iroh applies one setting
    to every relay of an endpoint). A public CA can then also vouch
    for the private relay's name.
  - An empty list or an unparsable certificate fails instead of being
    skipped.
- EndpointOptions.bind_port / EndpointBuilder.bind_port: bind 0.0.0.0
  and [::] to a fixed UDP port; refused with another bind address.
- EndpointOptions.external_addrs / EndpointBuilder.external_addr:
  advertise addresses such as the application's own router mapping
  (Endpoint.add_external_addr does this at runtime).

Tests check which chains each RelayTlsRoots accepts with the verifier
iroh builds from it: letsencrypt.org's chain (from
rustls-platform-verifier 0.7.0's test data, at a time it was valid)
and a certificate from a private test CA valid until 2126.

